->Queue is also used in tress for trversing it as whole. It is used in the Breadtf First Search(BFS) technique. 
->Specifically the Level order traversal which traverses the binary tree one level at a time. It's time complexity is O(n).
The process is very simple:-
    >Start by pushing the root into the queue.
    >Then if the queue is not empty, find its size.
    >Remove the node from the front of the queue, record its value and push its left and right child into the queue if they exist.
    >Repeat until all levels are traversed.

<------------------------------------------------------>
void levelOrder(TreeNode* root) {
    if ( root == NULL) return;

    queue<TreeNode*> q;
    q.push(root);

    int level = 0;

    while (!q.empty()) {
        int size = q.size();
        cout<<"Level " << level << ": ";

        for (int i = 0;i<size;i++) {
            TreeNode* current = q.front();
            q.pop();

            cout << current -> data<<" ";

            if (current->left)
                q.push(current->left);

            if (current->right)
            q.push(current->right);
        }
        cout << endl;
        level++;
    }
}
